Fix hpa escalation. Related to https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/16661

This eliminates the cross namespace escalation attack, but does not fix the API types themselves.

@kubernetes/kube-api @ncdc @liggitt @smarterclayton

Increase zero-limit pod RAM for spreading to 200 MB to match cluster. addon pods and represent less trivial fraction of typical machine RAM
(e.g. n1-standard-1).

@gmarek's comment got me thinking that probably the RAM I picked in the original PR was too low. The new RAM matches the RAM we're using for cluster addon pods (see #10653) and is a less trivial fraction of a typical minion machine (currently n1-standard-1 is 3.75GB and g1-small is 1.70 GB).

Addendum to #10661 for #10242

@erictune @gmarek @bprashanth

"KubeProxy should test kube-proxy" is extremely slow. Recent test results show it taking ~15m to run.

We should remove this from the regular test runs until it can be made faster.

@kubernetes/goog-testing @ArtfulCoder

Knock down the timeouts for gce, gce-slow, gke, and gke-slow. ... now that they run in parallel.

@k8s-oncall this should be a no-op, but should prevent the hangs you saw earlier.

cc @kubernetes/goog-testing

